      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Some people have noted the *opposite* problem now happens since the last update (build 772). With voice prioritization enabled, people are now very hard to hear from more than 2 meters away, even if nobody else is nearby. In the courtroom map for example, enabling voice prioritization makes it almost impossible to hear the judge or the opposite side.\n\nIf these reports are true, I'm glad they're doing at least something to address the problem, but it seems we're not quite there yet.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
