        "like": 8
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I disagree. Voice prioritization seemed to be a pretty complex and useful automated system. I don't want to have to constantly point at people and lower down 10 people's volumes just to hear 1 person, only to then have to repeat it when someone else speaks. In addition, voice prioritization is not meant to fix the fact that some people are super quiet and others are super loud.\n\nThey *can* accomplish similar goals, but ultimately they're two different systems and should be treated as such. Both are sorely needed, though.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
